  what: "The OOBE screen that tracks <b>device preparation → device setup → account setup</b> and can block desktop access until required apps/policies install.",
  why: "Guarantees a device is secured and equipped BEFORE the user can touch it.",
  how: "Devices > Enrollment > Windows > Enrollment Status Page: enable 'Show app and profile configuration progress', set timeout, 'Block device use until these required apps are installed' (choose blocking apps), allow reset/log collection on failure.",
  gotcha: "Only <b>required</b> (not available) apps selected as blocking apps block. Overlong timeouts frustrate users; failures at ESP commonly trace back to a failing blocking app or script.",
